{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1543778-i-ve-come-up-with-a-few-fomori-concept-ideas","id":1543778,"title":"I've come up with a few Fomori concept ideas","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-10-14T13:56:15-07:00","id":1543778,"title":"I've come up with a few Fomori concept ideas","content":"A woman named Beth who went to Dr. Veridian's Workout Program and came out as a special case. I got the idea from reading a little bit of Freak Legion and seeing a gigantic muscle babe fomor tearing a Stargazer in half.<br /> <br /> Equipment: none<br /> Attributes: strength 3, dexterity 2, stamina 3, charisma 3, manipulation 2, appearance (sexy) 5, perception 3, intelligence 3, wits 3<br /> Abilities: athletics 2, brawl 2, empathy 1, intimidation 3, subterfuge 2, drive 1<br /> Fomori Powers: mega-strength (+3) enhancement, body expansion, immunity to the delirium<br /> Taints: derangement (misandry, sadism, homicidal) mental de-evolution (+3; body expansion)<br /> <br /> <br /> A girl named Becky whose life changed after she started eating at O'Tolley's, she got addicted to the stuff and got hungrier and hungrier. Then everything took a turn when one day she was trying to save money because her habit was expensive but got hungry again, she discovered that she could swallow anything the size of a medium-sized dog or a small person. Possessed by a Bane of Consumption, from then on she started eating cats, dogs, small children and midgets. She looks relatively normal if a bit on the chubby side, she wears jeans and a t-shirt with a little bit of her gut poking out.<br /> <br /> Nature: predator<br /> Demeanor: confidant<br /> Equipment: none<br /> Attributes: strength 2, dexterity 2, stamina 2, charisma 2, manipulation 2, appearance 2, perception 3, intelligence 2, wits 2<br /> Abilities: athletics 1, brawl 1, dodge 1, empathy 1, streetwise 1, subterfuge 2, drive 1<br /> Fomori Powers: mouth of the wyrm, stomach pumper, immunity to the delirium, frog tongue<br /> Taints: addiction (Pentex food products, mouth of the wyrm; hourly cycle) derangement (pica, phagomania and cannibalism)<br /> Merits &amp; Flaws: hidden power<br /> <br /> <br /> A scaly guy named Joey aka Danger Joe aka Jarhead Joe who was a fomor since childhood because of the Action Bill Temporary Tattoos and other products, he was recruited later in life by Pentex. He is an Action Bill super-fan who keeps a shrine in his dorm.<br /> <br /> Nature: addict<br /> Demeanor: fanatic<br /> Equipment: Ithaca M-37 shotgun, armor-piercing shotgun rounds, Action Bill Special Police Badge, ID card, rank medallion, M-16 assault rifle with three magazines of ammunition, combat/survival knife with a compass in the handle, flak vest, a salary and a stipend<br /> Attributes: strength 3, dexterity 3, stamina 3, charisma 1, manipulation 2, appearance 1, perception 3, intelligence 1, wits 1<br /> Abilities: alertness 1, athletics 2, brawl 2, dodge 2, intimidation 3, streetwise 1, subterfuge 2, firearms 2, melee 2, stealth 3, survival 2, medicine 1<br /> Backgrounds: equipment/fetish 3, rank 1 (First Team Private), resources 1<br /> Fomori Powers: shadowplay, wall walking, nightmare command, horns, hide of the wyrm (5), immunity to the delirium<br /> Taints: brainwashed, derangement (temperamental, obsession), special diet (picky eater), severe allergy (soap and broccoli), addiction (crack cocaine, daily cycle), walking bomb<br /> Merits &amp; Flaws: deformity<br /> <br /> <br /> Some guy named Sid aka Big Smoke who became a Sicklung fomor via the Smoker's Bane program. Because he was a bit angry he was experimented on by Project Illiad for other purposes. This idea has been living in my head rent free for a while.<br /> <br /> Equipment: ID card, rank medallion, M-16 assault rifle with three magazines of ammunition, combat/survival knife with a compass in the handle, flak vest, a salary and a stipend<br /> Attributes: strength 2, dexterity 2, stamina 2, charisma 2, manipulation 2, appearance 2, perception 3, intelligence 2, wits 2<br /> Abilities: alertness 1, athletics 1, brawl 2, dodge 2, empathy 1, subterfuge 2, drive 1, firearms 2, melee 2, survival 2, medicine 1<br /> Backgrounds: equipment/fetish 0, rank 1 (First Team Private), resources 1<br /> Fomori Powers: noxious breath, immunity (airborne toxins), mega-strength (+3), hazardous breath (lethal smoke), immunity to the delirium<br /> Taints: breed prejudice (1), doomed (five years), derangement (temperamental), bane attractor, walking bomb, inner volcano","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28613,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","user":"Samuelalpha86","date":". 11-17-2025, 03:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","name":"Samuelalpha86","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-20T16:20:09-07:00","id":1544362,"title":"","content":"I have a hard time putting a lot of thought into combat type fomori, a lot of them won't last more than a turn or two, but I'll happily use <i>your </i>thoughts. These are great!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27296-devidramoth","name":"Devidramoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27296_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-20T19:24:38-07:00","id":1544370,"title":"","content":"Thank you! I needed an opinion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28613,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","user":"Samuelalpha86","date":". 10-20-2024, 10:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","name":"Samuelalpha86","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-20T20:02:42-07:00","id":1544372,"title":"","content":"I had to get real creative and do the math with the taints using the Freak Legion book. The book gave me ideas for what powers to use. The reason the last two have skills in firearms, melee, survival and medicine is because of Pentex First Team training. While the ID card, machine gun, medallion, survival knife and flak vest are given to all First Team members. They also have codenames because they're part of a First Team.<br /> <br /> I also used the first edition Book of the Wyrm for the Action Bill Special Police Badge as a sort of gimmick item to indicate the fomor's origin as to how he first got set on the path to corruption.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28613,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","user":"Samuelalpha86","date":". 10-23-2024, 10:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","name":"Samuelalpha86","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-21T10:00:17-07:00","id":1544402,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Devidramoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1543778-i-ve-come-up-with-a-few-fomori-concept-ideas?p=1544362#post1544362\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have a hard time putting a lot of thought into combat type fomori, a lot of them won't last more than a turn or two, but I'll happily use <i>your </i>thoughts. These are great!</div> </div> </div> </div>Out of curiosity, what were your previous ideas?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","name":"Samuelalpha86","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-23T22:38:18-07:00","id":1544628,"title":"","content":"I had a couple show up in an arc wherein some kindred had to skirt around getting involved in Garou politics. There was The Gorilla who had putrid blood, 10 health levels, a ton of soak dice, mega strength and was insensate to pain, taking only movement penalties and not dice penalties. I think he also had quick healing and the ability to roll to resist mental gifts/disciplines as though he had a humanity/rage/generation rating.<br /> <br /> He was supposed to be a minotaur, in a meta sense, not in canon. But the brujah just blood buffed strength activated auto-succ on potence and tried to ambush him with decent success.<br /> <br /> I also had a Devil Tiger who was able to make 'goblins' attacking the same city and the kindred had to deal with that. For lack of better guidance on how to make those from the KoTE books I have access to I decided to use freak legion. <br /> <br /> The idea was for a normal person who would just split open and their evil, corrupt hearts (by the devil tiger's reckoning) would become their new heads and they'd have claws, slightly enhanced durability and kindof as an offscreen thing, the ability to appear to be normal humans at a moment's notice. I considered giving them the pathetic ability on the basis of the human shells crying out for help, but decided that was unlikely to work on my PCs due to low humanity scores and didn't bother. Probably would've come up if they sent the coterie of Gangrel neonates after the Wan Kuei though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27296-devidramoth","name":"Devidramoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27296_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-26T20:10:25-07:00","id":1544830,"title":"","content":"You're aware that according to the Bygone Bestiary a normal gorilla would already have strength 5, dexterity 2, stamina 6, alertness 3, athletics 4, brawl 2, stealth 3 and an armor rating of 1, right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","name":"Samuelalpha86","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-01T23:10:17-07:00","id":1545196,"title":"","content":"Yes but I needed one that could walk around a chemical processing plant in a suit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27296-devidramoth","name":"Devidramoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27296_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-02T10:43:54-07:00","id":1545215,"title":"","content":"I know, you needed to make it a fomor, it's just that I'm surprised that it got defeated so easily. I just wanted to make sure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28613,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","user":"Samuelalpha86","date":". 11-18-2024, 06:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","name":"Samuelalpha86","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-18T14:54:57-08:00","id":1546090,"title":"","content":"Here's an idea, what if you make a Throwback Fomor with a Shotgun Penis?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28613,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","user":"Samuelalpha86","date":".  dialogue 11-18-2024, 06:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","name":"Samuelalpha86","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-18T16:38:20-08:00","id":1546100,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Samuelalpha86</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1543778-i-ve-come-up-with-a-few-fomori-concept-ideas?p=1546090#post1546090\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's an idea, what if you make a Throwback Fomor with a Shotgun Penis?</div> </div> </div> </div>...<br /> <br /> Where does he load the shells?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-19T07:46:11-08:00","id":1546129,"title":"","content":"It's supernatural he doesn't need to reload it's similar to the hazardous breath power allowing a fomor to spit bullets.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","name":"Samuelalpha86","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-16T19:32:29-08:00","id":1547084,"title":"","content":"What if you make a Fomor based on the Licker from the Resident Evil Franchise? They have Frog Tongue, Wall Walking, Mega-Strength (+3) and Claws with the Deformity Flaw.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28613,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","user":"Samuelalpha86","date":". 12-16-2024, 10:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","name":"Samuelalpha86","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-17T11:05:35-08:00","id":1547111,"title":"","content":"I like to think of Pentex First Teams as a mix between the Colonial Marines from Aliens and the Umbrella Security Service from Resident Evil.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","name":"Samuelalpha86","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-17T16:37:25-08:00","id":1547117,"title":"","content":"I just had an idea for a fomor based on the Hunter from Resident Evil. It has Hide of the Wyrm (3), Mega-Strength (3), Nimbleness, and Claws.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28613,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","user":"Samuelalpha86","date":". 12-20-2024, 10:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","name":"Samuelalpha86","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-19T07:24:19-08:00","id":1547149,"title":"","content":"What if you make a Gorehound based on Ghostface from Scream? Or maybe you can make a fomor based on Wolverine from Marvel Comics with the powers of claws, berserker, regeneration, brainwashed, and derangement (temperamental, homicidal) Taints and the hidden power Merit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28613,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","user":"Samuelalpha86","date":".  punctuation 12-21-2024, 02:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","name":"Samuelalpha86","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-19T11:13:01-08:00","id":1547150,"title":"","content":"Maybe a fomor based on the Tyrant from Resident Evil with mega-strength (5), nimbleness and regeneration, you can add claws and weak spot as a Taint for the normal tyrants or extra limbs (tentacles) if you want to recreate Nemesis.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28613,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","user":"Samuelalpha86","date":". 10-30-2025, 09:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","name":"Samuelalpha86","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-20T09:53:20-08:00","id":1547164,"title":"","content":"So, any thoughts on my idea of using other franchises as inspiration?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28613,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","user":"Samuelalpha86","date":". 12-21-2024, 07:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","name":"Samuelalpha86","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-12-24T17:06:47-08:00","id":1547226,"title":"","content":"Okay since nobody is responding I'm gonna recreate the Fomori from Hunter: Urban Legends.<br /> <br /> They have Frog Tongue, Water Breathing and Nimbleness with the Deformity Flaw.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28613,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28613-samuelalpha86","user":"Samuelalpha86","date":". 12-24-2024, 08:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"use